    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.26395898591549294,
        "y0": 0.8792032111475863,
        "x1": 0.4882399161690141,
        "y1": 0.8857609458371208
      },
      "text": "Hampole, MS. Bowes, p. 180.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "heading",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.05627346478873239,
        "y0": 0.8899035566606897,
        "x1": 0.2692308784225352,
        "y1": 0.8986689090797587
      },
      "text": "SETLINGS. Saplings.",
      "html": null,
      "level": 1,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07813509859154928,
        "y0": 0.9050376641737932,
        "x1": 0.4882431549295776,
        "y1": 0.9488227478394496
      },
      "text": "For such as be yet infirm and weak, and newly planted in the religion of Christ, and have taken no sure root in the same, are easily moved as young tellings. Becon's fVorkSfP. 10.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5210356056338028,
        "y0": 0.08050917517241389,
        "x1": 0.8315485358873241,
        "y1": 0.09095033350364572
      },
      "text": "SETNESSE. A decree. Heame.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5206307605633802,
        "y0": 0.09526737063586214,
        "x1": 0.9505729865915492,
        "y1": 0.11695874854749863
      },
      "text": "SET-OPE. Anything by means of which a gate or door is set or kept open.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5206307605633802,
        "y0": 0.12239945667448285,
        "x1": 0.7615168162253518,
        "y1": 0.1305908879071017
      },
      "text": "SETS. The plaits of ruffs.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5202259154929577,
        "y0": 0.1342802786206898,
        "x1": 0.9497730127323941,
        "y1": 0.15748941040654357
      },
      "text": "SET-SPEECH. A speech carefully prepared and studied before it is deUvered in public.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.16213251584413796,
        "x1": 0.7445068457464792,
        "y1": 0.17072985199577445
      },
      "text": "SETTE. Ruled. Scott.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5194162253521126,
        "y0": 0.17501757881241384,
        "x1": 0.9048238742535211,
        "y1": 0.18444537163888608
      },
      "text": "SETTEN-ON. Short in growth. North.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5190113802816901,
        "y0": 0.18891497076965527,
        "x1": 0.949361690140845,
        "y1": 0.2382070900001887
      },
      "text": "SETTER. (1) To cut the dew-lap of an ox or cow, into which helleboraster, called setterwork, being put, an issue is made for ill-humours to vent themselves. North.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5177968450704225,
        "y0": 0.24237134724137935,
        "x1": 0.7303405070422535,
        "y1": 0.2521380336242531
      },
      "text": "(2) An accuser. Coles.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5177968450704225,
        "y0": 0.25594017545517256,
        "x1": 0.9481552518309863,
        "y1": 0.2651310297058496
      },
      "text": "SETTER-GRASS. Theherb bear's-foot. Yorksh.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5169871549295774,
        "y0": 0.2701313162248276,
        "x1": 0.8659692734647886,
        "y1": 0.29214542974672447
      },
      "text": "Spelt setyrgrise in Nominale MS. SETTER-OUT. An editor, or author.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5169871549295774,
        "y0": 0.2965490890841379,
        "x1": 0.947338274478873,
        "y1": 0.3185611843725718
      },
      "text": "SETTING. The west, so caUed because the quarter of the setting sun.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5169871549295774,
        "y0": 0.3228928758786208,
        "x1": 0.9473407035492953,
        "y1": 0.3457427352880873
      },
      "text": "SETTING-DOWN. Said of a hawk when put into the mew. Gent. Rec. ii. 63.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5161774647887324,
        "y0": 0.34959725615310344,
        "x1": 0.9469326197183098,
        "y1": 0.37244525646034093
      },
      "text": "SETTING-PIN. A dibble. Glouc. \"Debbyll or settyng stycke,\" Huloet, 1552.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5157726197183098,
        "y0": 0.37637414068965525,
        "x1": 0.9465277746478873,
        "y1": 0.3994140360259855
      },
      "text": "SETTING-STICK. A stick used for making the plaits or sets of ruffs.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5149629295774648,
        "y0": 0.4040328068965518,
        "x1": 0.7833784500281686,
        "y1": 0.41273377217257834
      },
      "text": "SETTLE. (1) To fall in price.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8068562253521125,
        "y0": 0.40633876951724146,
        "x1": 0.8517940281690138,
        "y1": 0.41277748382150103
      },
      "text": "Line.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5145580845070422,
        "y0": 0.4167491871875862,
        "x1": 0.9453164781971829,
        "y1": 0.4544628162622664
      },
      "text": "(2) A long seat, generally one with a long back to it. North. It is an archaism. See Setille. SETTLE-BED. A folding bed.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5141532394366197,
        "y0": 0.45778710997241384,
        "x1": 0.9449092040563379,
        "y1": 0.48054874517260243
      },
      "text": "SETTLE-STONES. Stones at the edge of a gutter in a cow-house. North.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5133435492957746,
        "y0": 0.4854093010344828,
        "x1": 0.7165757746478872,
        "y1": 0.49417080425360455
      },
      "text": "SEU. Suit. Heame.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5141532394366197,
        "y0": 0.49729717517241384,
        "x1": 0.943284155943662,
        "y1": 0.5342541530120651
      },
      "text": "SEUGH. A wet ditch; a drain. North. \" The towne sinke, the common sew,\" Nomenclator, 1585, p. 391.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5125338591549295,
        "y0": 0.5382753054813794,
        "x1": 0.7477528935211267,
        "y1": 0.5475609854017368
      },
      "text": "SEUNE. Seven. Cumb.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.512129014084507,
        "y0": 0.5512842203986208,
        "x1": 0.9428809302535214,
        "y1": 0.5743848175130157
      },
      "text": "SEUREMENT. Security, generally used in the legal sense. (A.-N.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5117241690140845,
        "y0": 0.578484543702069,
        "x1": 0.831950142197183,
        "y1": 0.5880548021045162
      },
      "text": "SEURETEE. Certainty. (A.-N.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5113193239436619,
        "y0": 0.5919389113255173,
        "x1": 0.9416680144225354,
        "y1": 0.6155347669768697
      },
      "text": "SEVEN-NIGHT. A week. This word occurs in The French Alphabet, 1615, p. 18.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5700218591549295,
        "y0": 0.6184589682220689,
        "x1": 0.8064481415211264,
        "y1": 0.626453305340216
      },
      "text": "He levyth not oon sevevyghte.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5105096338028168,
        "y0": 0.631660507586207,
        "x1": 0.9416672047323943,
        "y1": 0.6791203104470149
      },
      "text": "MS. Cantab. Ff. ii. 38, f. 63. SEVEN-YEAR. \" Has been a vile thief this seven year,\" Shakespeare. It was a proverbial expression for a long time.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5684024788732394,
        "y0": 0.6840299792565517,
        "x1": 0.7538279986478873,
        "y1": 0.6909990851967239
      },
      "text": "O, the body of a Gorge,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5684024788732394,
        "y0": 0.6956914844827587,
        "x1": 0.770825014084507,
        "y1": 0.7036652557897045
      },
      "text": "I wold I had them heare ;",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5679976338028169,
        "y0": 0.7079489321227587,
        "x1": 0.7951197667605632,
        "y1": 0.714825806263093
      },
      "text": "In faith, I wold chope them,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5675927887323943,
        "y0": 0.718667738222069,
        "x1": 0.8853953593239435,
        "y1": 0.7262079947302735
      },
      "text": "Thay ware not so hack this seven yeere '",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6574683943661972,
        "y0": 0.7316716179834483,
        "x1": 0.9388357183098591,
        "y1": 0.7391254770966504
      },
      "text": "Mariage of Witt and TVisdomet 1579.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5675927887323943,
        "y0": 0.7462427593889656,
        "x1": 0.8449043747605631,
        "y1": 0.7524569887891036
      },
      "text": "I can then thanke Sensuall Apetyte",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5675927887323943,
        "y0": 0.7562419495365518,
        "x1": 0.8833751824225351,
        "y1": 0.7651712557398213
      },
      "text": "That is the best daunce without a pype",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5671879436619718,
        "y0": 0.768136018502069,
        "x1": 0.7748734647887323,
        "y1": 0.7757988564069953
      },
      "text": "That I saw this seven yere.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6522054084507042,
        "y0": 0.7817341804634482,
        "x1": 0.9388357183098591,
        "y1": 0.7889318908897539
      },
      "text": "Interlude of the Four Elements, n. d.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5080805633802816,
        "y0": 0.7934757426855172,
        "x1": 0.9392405633802816,
        "y1": 0.8566211623406019
      },
      "text": "SEVERALS. Portions of common assigned for a term to a particular proprietor, the other commoners waiving for the time their right of common over them. See Hunter on Shakespeare, i. 267.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5072708732394365,
        "y0": 0.8602822203986207,
        "x1": 0.9384316829295775,
        "y1": 0.896786934018749
      },
      "text": "SEVERY. A division or compartment of a vaulted ceihng. \" Severous of a howse,\" MS. Dictionary, 1540.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5072708732394365,
        "y0": 0.9003776224675862,
        "x1": 0.7825655211267605,
        "y1": 0.9105983046828573
      },
      "text": "SEW. (1) Same as Assue, q. v.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5072708732394365,
        "y0": 0.9153222475503447,
        "x1": 0.672451710422535,
        "y1": 0.9241529301759771
      },
      "text": "(2) Sowed. Line.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "list",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5072708732394365,
        "y0": 0.9280833693641378,
        "x1": 0.9372098605070421,
        "y1": 0.9502727040156834
      },
      "text": "To wipe the ))eak, a term in ancient hawking given by Berners.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
  ],
